## Screens & components annotated

- **Header (all screens)**: `nav.*` — logo, Find Jobs, Employer, Post a Job as `navigation` with targets; nav bar as `region`
- **Index (job seeker home)**: `jobs.*` — hero active-jobs count and results count/empty state as `observable`; filter panel (`jobs.filters`) with search `input`, three `select` triggers carrying `data-semtag-options` built from the same arrays that render the menus, option ids on every `SelectItem`, clear-filters `action` — all with `data-semtag-controls="jobs.list"`; job grid as `collection` with items `jobs.list.item.<job.id>` (navigation) plus per-item salary observable
- **Job detail**: `job.detail.*` — back link, title/company/location/salary/posted/industry/type observables, description `region`, skills `collection` (`.item.<slug>`), plus the not-found state and its browse link
- **Application form**: `application.form.*` — name/email/phone/message inputs with `application.*` state keys, submit `action`
- **Employer dashboard**: `dashboard.*` — stats observables (`employer.jobs.count`, `employer.applications.count`), jobs `collection` with item id on each title, per-item `toggle-applications` (state `open`/`closed`) and `delete-job` controls, delete-confirm dialog (region + confirm/cancel actions), nested applications `collection` per job with `dashboard.applications.item.<app.id>` name/email/message observables, and both empty states
- **Post job form**: `post-job.form.*` — all inputs/selects (with options), skills chip `collection` with per-chip `.remove` actions, submit/cancel
- **NotFound**: `notfound.*` message + home link

## Id namespaces
`nav`, `jobs`, `job.detail`, `application`, `dashboard`, `dashboard.applications`, `post-job`, `notfound`. Shared state keys connect controls to displays (e.g. `filters.*` on selects, `job.applications.count` on toggle count and empty message).

## Notes
- **One helper added**: `src/lib/semtag.ts` (`semtagSlug`) — pure string function to build stable ids from values like "San Francisco, CA" / "Node.js"; no behavior change. Uniqueness at runtime holds: job/app ids are unique db ids, skill lists are deduplicated by the app, and each select's options are distinct.
- **Ancestry verified by reading**: every `collection` container is a DOM ancestor of its `.item.` children. The delete-confirm dialog renders in a Radix portal (outside the collection), which is fine — only one renders at a time and its ids stay unique.
- **Deliberately unhinted**: decorative hero stats ("1,000+ Companies"), per-card badges on the list (available on detail), per-application phone/date, and the long description text (region only — capturing it would bloat every snapshot).
